  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Connecting Voice(s) 2: Multi-Country L&amp;L</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Constellation, as the global Linking and Learning Facilitator, will continue to support the multi-country grantees of Voice in Africa and Asia, in line with the programme closure plans and transitions in promoting the Power of NoW-Us. For the remaining months, The Constellation will organise a Global Link and Learn Festival, round up the joint learning resources process, and document the entire journey in the project.

Continuing its approach since the beginning, The Constellation shall maintain safe spaces for learning conversations between the multi-country grantees in spite of cultural, geographical, and thematic differences, facilitate identification of strengths and areas for improvement based on the themes identified by grantees and rightsholder groups, co-create capacity building processes, facilitate online and offline learning events, facilitate an online platform, facilitate Communities of Practice (CoP) who build joint knowledge, and ensure that rightsholders&#x2019; voice and lens come forwardin publications and media expressions that are products of the learning process.</narrative>
  </description>
