  <participating-org role="4" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Constellation for AIDS Competen</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Constellation is an organisation in service of a network of people who are acting locally to create a better world, aiming to build capacities of communities and organisations to develop their vision, analyse their problems, and formulate solutions, based on their own strengths and resources. Their discovery began 23 years ago with HIV/AIDS when people in Thailand, Uganda, and Brazil had begun to address this issue publicly and to recognise that it was theirs to deal with. They took ownership of their response to HIV and it became the basis of a local response that reduced the impact of the epidemic. It also led to the foundation of The Constellation in 2004.

The Constellation trains and accompanies local people through an  innovative learning process called SALT-CLCP to stimulate local action, and facilitates internal and external learning and sharing of experience with a peer-to-peer strategy to exchange knowledge and open opportunities for the emergence of new knowledge.

Over almost 17 years, the organisation has trained more than3,000 local facilitators and have successfully stimulated and accompanied various groups in a journey toward development of Local Response through more than 120 partnerships.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
